WEBVTT

00:00:02.002 --> 00:00:03.435
Though it was
a blatant violation

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:04.561
of the Prime Directive,

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:06.605
Kirk saved the Pelosians
from extinction,

00:00:06.673 --> 00:00:08.106
just as he had the Baezians

00:00:08.174 --> 00:00:09.937
and the Chenari,
many years earlier.

00:00:10.010 --> 00:00:14.379
Finally, in the year 2270,

00:00:14.447 --> 00:00:17.348
Kirk completed
his historic five-year mission,

00:00:17.417 --> 00:00:20.477
and one of the greatest chapters
in Starfleet history

00:00:20.553 --> 00:00:21.611
came to a close.

00:00:21.688 --> 00:00:24.122
A new chapter began

00:00:24.190 --> 00:00:26.454
when Kirk regained command
of the Enterprise.

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.653
How many more chapters
are there?

00:00:28.728 --> 00:00:30.286
Thirty-four.

00:00:30.363 --> 00:00:33.890
This was supposed to be
a 20-minute presentation.

00:00:33.967 --> 00:00:36.197
I was trying to be thorough.

00:00:36.269 --> 00:00:38.430
I-I could shorten the report.

00:00:38.505 --> 00:00:39.972
That won't be necessary.

00:00:40.073 --> 00:00:42.837
You obviously know
the subject matter.

00:00:42.909 --> 00:00:44.536
Congratulations, Cadet.

00:00:44.611 --> 00:00:47.978
You have just passed
Early Starfleet History.

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:49.276
Thank you, Captain.

00:00:58.858 --> 00:01:01.486
I would've failed him.

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:03.756
Kirk may have been
a lowly human,

00:01:03.830 --> 00:01:05.457
but at least he had pizzazz.

00:01:05.532 --> 00:01:07.329
That report made him sound
about as exciting

00:01:07.400 --> 00:01:09.334
as a Vulcan funeral dirge.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:10.926
Janeway to Security.

00:01:11.004 --> 00:01:12.665
Don't bother.

00:01:12.739 --> 00:01:14.934
I trapped your crew
in a temporal loop.

00:01:15.008 --> 00:01:16.270
They keep experiencing

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:18.401
the last 30 seconds
over and over.

00:01:18.478 --> 00:01:20.776
Almost as monotonous
as drone boy's essay.

00:01:20.847 --> 00:01:21.905
Who are you?

00:01:21.981 --> 00:01:25.747
I know he's grown
since you last saw him, Kathy,

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:29.277
but don't tell me you can't see
the family resemblance.

00:01:29.355 --> 00:01:31.585
This is my son...

00:01:31.658 --> 00:01:33.626
Q.

00:03:24.504 --> 00:03:26.335
I'm a little hurt you
didn't recognize Junior.

00:03:26.406 --> 00:03:28.431
You are his godmother,
after all.

00:03:28.508 --> 00:03:30.305
The last time I saw
him, he was an infant.

00:03:30.376 --> 00:03:31.934
Four years ago in human time.

00:03:32.045 --> 00:03:33.512
You called me "adorable."

00:03:33.580 --> 00:03:35.070
You remember?

00:03:35.148 --> 00:03:36.274
I may have looked
like an infant,

00:03:36.349 --> 00:03:37.577
but I was still a Q.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.811
Maybe you should've picked
a better godparent.

00:03:39.886 --> 00:03:41.444
I wonder if it's too late
to ask Jean-Luc.

00:03:41.521 --> 00:03:42.453
What do you want, Q?

00:03:42.522 --> 00:03:44.956
Oh, Junior's taking
a little vacation

00:03:45.058 --> 00:03:45.956
from the Continuum.

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.356
I recommended
he spend it with you.

00:03:47.427 --> 00:03:48.359
Why?

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.056
Oh, he's always been fascinated

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.189
by the old man's stories
about humanity.

00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.099
I thought it was time he has
some firsthand experience.

00:03:56.169 --> 00:03:58.637
I am flattered
that you would entrust me

00:03:58.705 --> 00:04:01.230
with your firstborn,
but I really don't have time.

00:04:01.307 --> 00:04:04.003
He's as quiet as a Z yznian
church mouse.

00:04:04.077 --> 00:04:05.669
You'll forget he's even here.

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.745
Well, if you're going to stay,

00:04:10.817 --> 00:04:13.877
we'll need to lay down
a few ground rules.

00:04:16.956 --> 00:04:20.790
I make my own rules.

00:04:23.062 --> 00:04:25.394
I'm not detecting either Q.

00:04:25.465 --> 00:04:27.092
I want to be alerted
if they resurface.

00:04:27.166 --> 00:04:28.895
Keep running scans.

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:30.697
Scan, scan, scan.

00:04:30.770 --> 00:04:32.465
That's all you people ever do.

00:04:32.538 --> 00:04:34.802
I've been through every deck
on this ship,

00:04:34.874 --> 00:04:36.603
and do you know what I've seen?

00:04:36.676 --> 00:04:39.236
Bipeds pushing buttons,

00:04:39.312 --> 00:04:41.780
bipeds replacing relays,

00:04:41.848 --> 00:04:43.782
bipeds running diagnostics.

00:04:43.850 --> 00:04:45.943
When are you going to do
something interesting?

00:04:46.019 --> 00:04:48.544
Say hello to Q, everyone.

00:04:50.189 --> 00:04:55.491
We could fly into fluidic space
and fight species 8472...

00:04:55.561 --> 00:04:58.086
or we could detonate
a few Omega molecules.

00:04:58.164 --> 00:05:00.359
What do you say?

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:02.025
No.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:04.897
20 minutes observing humanity.

00:05:05.004 --> 00:05:06.335
I'm already bored.

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:09.341
I guess I'm just going
to have to amuse myself.

00:05:10.009 --> 00:05:11.738
Torres to the Captain.

00:05:11.811 --> 00:05:13.574
I need you in Engineering.

00:05:29.362 --> 00:05:31.125
Once dance, B'Elanna!

00:05:31.197 --> 00:05:33.290
That's all I ask... one dance.

00:05:43.609 --> 00:05:45.873
If he doesn't stop
his little light show,

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.412
the warp core's going to breach.

00:05:47.480 --> 00:05:48.947
Relax. It's a party.

00:05:49.048 --> 00:05:50.709
This party is over.

00:05:50.783 --> 00:05:53.479
Get your... guests off my ship.

00:05:53.553 --> 00:05:55.282
I like you, Aunt Kathy.

00:05:55.355 --> 00:05:58.085
You've got gumption,
but what you don't have

00:05:58.157 --> 00:06:01.058
is unlimited control
of space, matter and time,

00:06:01.127 --> 00:06:03.823
which means I give
the orders around here.

00:06:06.766 --> 00:06:08.631
I could assemble a security team

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.192
and attempt to take
Engineering by force.

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:12.897
We all know
that wouldn't do any good.

00:06:12.972 --> 00:06:14.564
Besides, I'll bet that's exactly

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.870
the kind of reaction
he's hoping for.

00:06:16.943 --> 00:06:20.470
He's doing everything he can
to get under our skin.

00:06:20.546 --> 00:06:22.411
If we deny him the satisfaction
of a response,

00:06:22.482 --> 00:06:26.475
he may become bored
and return to the Continuum.

00:06:29.155 --> 00:06:31.521
Talk about perfection.

00:06:33.059 --> 00:06:34.924
If you're attempting
to embarrass me,

00:06:34.994 --> 00:06:36.325
you won't succeed.

00:06:36.396 --> 00:06:38.091
I'm just observing humanity.

00:06:42.301 --> 00:06:45.202
Aren't you going
to scamper away,

00:06:45.271 --> 00:06:47.796
make some futile attempt
to cover yourself?

00:07:04.757 --> 00:07:06.224
Coffee, black.

00:07:06.292 --> 00:07:08.192
Make it yourself.

00:07:08.261 --> 00:07:10.729
You can thank Q's son.

00:07:10.797 --> 00:07:13.891
He thought the computer
needed more personality.

00:07:13.966 --> 00:07:15.331
Charming.

00:07:16.769 --> 00:07:21.638
I've been giving some thought
to the Q situation.

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:25.507
Maybe ignoring him
isn't the best solution.

00:07:25.578 --> 00:07:27.876
I'm open to suggestions.

00:07:30.450 --> 00:07:31.576
He may be omnipotent,

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:34.347
but he's still a young man
in need of guidance.

00:07:34.420 --> 00:07:37.753
Perhaps if someone were
to approach him as a friend.

00:07:37.824 --> 00:07:39.223
You think he needs a mentor.

00:07:39.292 --> 00:07:40.224
Exactly.

00:07:40.293 --> 00:07:41.726
Are you volunteering?

00:07:41.794 --> 00:07:44.558
Well, I am good with children.

00:07:44.630 --> 00:07:48.031
Q is no ordinary child.

00:07:48.100 --> 00:07:50.694
I'm no ordinary mentor.

00:07:58.010 --> 00:08:00.137
Can I help you, Kitchen Rat?

00:08:00.213 --> 00:08:03.114
I thought you and I could
spend some time together.

00:08:03.182 --> 00:08:05.548
Ha! Excellent maneuver.

00:08:05.618 --> 00:08:06.880
What are you watching?

00:08:07.019 --> 00:08:08.646
What's it look like?

00:08:08.721 --> 00:08:11.383
It's a battle between
the Vojeans and the Wyngari.

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:15.086
We passed through that region
a few months ago.

00:08:17.897 --> 00:08:18.886
They were at peace.

00:08:18.998 --> 00:08:20.898
Not anymore.

00:08:20.967 --> 00:08:22.264
Watch this.

00:08:25.605 --> 00:08:27.129
You have to stop this.

00:08:27.206 --> 00:08:29.766
It's not like
there's anything else to do.

00:08:29.842 --> 00:08:31.867
We could play Kadis-Kot.

00:08:31.944 --> 00:08:33.775
Are there explosions
in Kadis-Kot?

00:08:33.846 --> 00:08:35.473
Well, no...

00:08:35.548 --> 00:08:36.480
Well, then I'm not interested.

00:08:42.955 --> 00:08:47.051
Instead of hurting people,
maybe you could help them.

00:08:47.126 --> 00:08:51.187
The Wyngari are suffering
a food shortage on their world.

00:08:51.264 --> 00:08:53.892
Maybe you could use
your powers to...

00:08:53.966 --> 00:08:55.729
You know what, Talaxian?

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:58.326
You talk too much.

00:08:58.404 --> 00:09:03.501
His jaw's been fused
and his vocal cords removed.

00:09:03.576 --> 00:09:06.204
I might be able to undo some
of the cosmetic damage,

00:09:06.279 --> 00:09:09.544
but only Q can restore
his voice.

00:09:09.615 --> 00:09:11.879
Janeway to the Bridge.
Report.

00:09:11.984 --> 00:09:16.353
I've got a surprise for you,
Captain. Come see.

00:09:17.924 --> 00:09:19.983
Q said I should pay attention

00:09:20.059 --> 00:09:22.823
to how you humans
act under pressure.

00:09:29.368 --> 00:09:31.495
Is this enough pressure?

00:09:42.381 --> 00:09:43.780
We're venting plasma.

00:09:43.849 --> 00:09:46.875
Reroute power to aft shields
and return fire.

00:09:46.953 --> 00:09:48.818
You're just prolonging
the inevitable.

00:09:48.888 --> 00:09:50.446
We've defeated the Borg before.

00:09:50.523 --> 00:09:51.785
We'll do it again.

00:09:51.857 --> 00:09:54.690
Not this time.

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:56.921
Weapons are off-line.

00:09:57.029 --> 00:09:58.257
I'm losing thrusters.

00:09:58.331 --> 00:09:59.355
Shields are down.

00:10:12.778 --> 00:10:15.246
We were just getting
to the good part.

00:10:15.314 --> 00:10:17.179
If the Continuum's
told you once,

00:10:17.249 --> 00:10:19.308
they've told you
a thousand times:

00:10:19.385 --> 00:10:23.321
Don't provoke the Borg!

00:10:23.389 --> 00:10:25.721
Now... I want you to give
Aunt Kathy your word,

00:10:25.791 --> 00:10:26.951
you won't do it again.

00:10:27.059 --> 00:10:29.186
Oh, he won't do it again,

00:10:29.261 --> 00:10:31.855
because he's leaving now.

00:10:31.931 --> 00:10:33.091
Excuse us, son.

00:10:33.165 --> 00:10:36.566
The grownups
need a moment in private.

00:10:40.106 --> 00:10:42.233
He isn't so bad,
once you get to know him.

00:10:42.308 --> 00:10:43.570
He's just misunderstood.

00:10:43.643 --> 00:10:45.804
He tried to kill my crew.

00:10:45.878 --> 00:10:46.810
No one was hurt.

00:10:46.879 --> 00:10:48.346
I-I repaired the damage
to your ship.

00:10:48.414 --> 00:10:51.144
I even gave your pet Talaxian
his vocal cords back.

00:10:51.217 --> 00:10:53.412
Everything's exactly as it was.

00:10:53.486 --> 00:10:56.421
And how long do you think
it will take your... son

00:10:56.489 --> 00:10:59.481
to come up with another way
to amuse himself?

00:10:59.558 --> 00:11:00.786
Oh...

00:11:02.194 --> 00:11:04.924
If you knew he was dangerous,
why did you send him here?

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:07.625
Ah, is this another
lesson for humanity?

00:11:07.700 --> 00:11:09.895
It's supposed to be
a lesson for him.

00:11:09.969 --> 00:11:11.527
Think back to my last visit.

00:11:11.604 --> 00:11:13.765
I made you the offer
of a lifetime.

00:11:13.839 --> 00:11:14.771
Asking me to mate with you

00:11:14.840 --> 00:11:16.705
was hardly the offer
of a lifetime.

00:11:16.776 --> 00:11:17.708
If you hadn't turned me down,

00:11:17.777 --> 00:11:19.142
I wouldn't
have been forced to mate

00:11:19.211 --> 00:11:20.178
- with that other Q.
- Oh, get to the point.

00:11:20.246 --> 00:11:21.304
My point is,

00:11:21.380 --> 00:11:24.042
Junior was supposed to inspire
peace and compassion,

00:11:24.116 --> 00:11:26.778
but instead of order,
he's brought chaos.

00:11:26.852 --> 00:11:29.787
He's been starting wars
among innocent species,

00:11:29.855 --> 00:11:32.187
tampering
with primordial gene pools,

00:11:32.258 --> 00:11:34.852
punching holes
in the fabric of space-time.

00:11:34.927 --> 00:11:37.452
Where's his mother been
during all this?

00:11:37.530 --> 00:11:39.293
She's been so humiliated
by his antics,

00:11:39.365 --> 00:11:40.627
she's disowned him,

00:11:40.700 --> 00:11:42.600
and she's blamed me
for everything.

00:11:42.668 --> 00:11:45.637
I've managed to undo
most of the damage,

00:11:45.705 --> 00:11:47.502
but that wasn't good
enough for the Continuum.

00:11:47.573 --> 00:11:50.303
They're hounding me to
straighten the boy out.

00:11:50.376 --> 00:11:52.367
That's why I brought him here,

00:11:52.445 --> 00:11:55.642
in hopes that your vaunted
Starfleet ideals

00:11:55.715 --> 00:11:56.977
would rub off on him.

00:11:57.083 --> 00:11:58.778
Obviously, that hasn't happened.

00:11:58.851 --> 00:12:01.081
You can't just dump
your child on someone

00:12:01.153 --> 00:12:02.745
and hope he learns something.

00:12:02.822 --> 00:12:03.754
I can't?

00:12:03.823 --> 00:12:05.154
He needs to be parented.

00:12:05.224 --> 00:12:07.488
And how exactly am I
supposed to do that?

00:12:07.560 --> 00:12:09.585
Q is the first child
born in the Continuum,

00:12:09.662 --> 00:12:11.721
which makes me the first parent.

00:12:11.797 --> 00:12:13.924
I don't even know
where to begin.

00:12:14.033 --> 00:12:16.968
You could start
by spending time with him.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:19.564
Parenthood is more

00:12:19.638 --> 00:12:22.505
than just cleaning up
your child's messes.

00:12:22.575 --> 00:12:24.543
You need to set an example.

00:12:24.610 --> 00:12:26.840
It's the only way he'll learn.

00:12:26.912 --> 00:12:27.936
Of course.

00:12:28.047 --> 00:12:30.914
Once he begins to know me
better, he'll idolize me.

00:12:30.983 --> 00:12:32.644
Then he'll do anything I say.

00:12:32.718 --> 00:12:34.481
Kathy.

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:37.416
You're a genius.

00:12:40.326 --> 00:12:42.453
I've made a full sensor sweep.

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:46.157
There's no sign
of any more Borg vessels.

00:12:47.199 --> 00:12:48.325
The boy?

00:12:48.400 --> 00:12:49.332
He's gone.

00:12:50.402 --> 00:12:52.370
I am going to my quarters.

00:12:52.438 --> 00:12:54.998
You have the Bridge.

00:13:01.981 --> 00:13:04.006
I take it back...
you're not a genius.

00:13:04.083 --> 00:13:05.209
Mm. I should've known better

00:13:05.284 --> 00:13:06.751
than to take the advice
of a human.

00:13:06.819 --> 00:13:07.911
Q!

00:13:08.020 --> 00:13:09.612
Your brilliant plan didn't work.

00:13:09.688 --> 00:13:11.178
I smothered the boy
with attention,

00:13:11.257 --> 00:13:12.747
spent every waking moment

00:13:12.825 --> 00:13:14.918
with him,
but things only got worse.

00:13:14.994 --> 00:13:17.792
You've been gone
for less than ten minutes.

00:13:17.863 --> 00:13:20.889
On your temporal plane, maybe,
but in Q time,

00:13:20.966 --> 00:13:22.831
we've spent years together.

00:13:22.902 --> 00:13:25.598
Now he's embarrassed
to be seen with me,

00:13:25.671 --> 00:13:27.104
and it's all your fault.

00:13:27.173 --> 00:13:28.333
My fault?

00:13:28.407 --> 00:13:31.968
Tell me how you plan to rectify
the situation.

00:13:34.046 --> 00:13:36.674
What happened
after you left Voyager?

00:13:36.749 --> 00:13:38.717
Well, Q got away from me

00:13:38.784 --> 00:13:42.948
and rearranged the tectonic
plates on Bozel Prime.

00:13:43.022 --> 00:13:44.580
Did you punish him?

00:13:44.657 --> 00:13:46.750
Well, I tried to get him
to apologize

00:13:46.826 --> 00:13:48.418
to all 16 billion Bozelians,

00:13:48.494 --> 00:13:50.962
but he got angry
and stopped talking to me.

00:13:51.063 --> 00:13:52.655
So you gave in to him.

00:13:52.731 --> 00:13:56.667
I told him he could shift
as many continents as he liked,

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:58.703
as long as no one got hurt.

00:13:58.771 --> 00:14:02.764
You're not going to do your son
any favors by indulging him.

00:14:04.143 --> 00:14:05.235
You need to make him understand

00:14:05.311 --> 00:14:08.180
that there are consequences
to his actions.

00:14:08.247 --> 00:14:10.272
Consequences?

00:14:10.349 --> 00:14:11.611
Hmm.

00:14:11.684 --> 00:14:14.278
Kathy, I take it back.

00:14:14.353 --> 00:14:16.981
You are a genius.

00:14:24.697 --> 00:14:26.324
I think that's long enough.

00:14:30.035 --> 00:14:31.935
What was that for?

00:14:32.037 --> 00:14:33.436
What's wrong...
you didn't enjoy life

00:14:33.505 --> 00:14:35.029
as an Oprelian amoeba?

00:14:35.107 --> 00:14:38.838
No. I was shapeless and slimy.

00:14:38.911 --> 00:14:41.004
The only thing to eat
was paramecia.

00:14:42.381 --> 00:14:43.507
Sounds unpleasant.

00:14:43.582 --> 00:14:45.447
I'm sure you'll do
whatever you can

00:14:45.517 --> 00:14:47.576
to avoid returning
to that petri dish.

00:14:47.653 --> 00:14:49.177
What are you talking about?

00:14:49.255 --> 00:14:52.383
The Continuum and I
have come to an agreement

00:14:52.458 --> 00:14:53.720
about your future.

00:14:53.792 --> 00:14:57.125
Either you become
an upstanding citizen

00:14:57.196 --> 00:14:58.959
of the cosmos, or
you'll be sentenced

00:14:59.031 --> 00:15:01.556
to eternity as an amoeba.

00:15:01.634 --> 00:15:03.499
How's that for consequences?

00:15:03.569 --> 00:15:07.869
You'd turn your own son
into a microscopic life-form?

00:15:07.940 --> 00:15:09.908
You have one week
to change your ways.

00:15:10.009 --> 00:15:11.772
I suggest
you make the most of it.

00:15:12.811 --> 00:15:14.073
Fine.

00:15:14.146 --> 00:15:16.307
I'll see you in seven days.

00:15:20.152 --> 00:15:23.747
We've temporarily
relieved you of your powers,

00:15:23.822 --> 00:15:25.380
to ensure that you're

00:15:25.457 --> 00:15:27.049
on your best behavior
with the Captain.

00:15:27.126 --> 00:15:29.287
You're leaving me here?

00:15:29.361 --> 00:15:30.623
I thought we agreed

00:15:30.696 --> 00:15:33.130
that you were going to take
a more active role.

00:15:33.198 --> 00:15:36.167
I'd like to, Kathy,

00:15:36.235 --> 00:15:39.432
but we both know that you're
a million times the parent I am.

00:15:39.505 --> 00:15:40.665
I'm not a parent.

00:15:40.739 --> 00:15:42.832
Well, maybe not
in a biological sense,

00:15:42.908 --> 00:15:45.308
but you're certainly
a mommy to this crew.

00:15:45.377 --> 00:15:48.835
Just look how quickly
you housebroke that Borg drone.

00:15:48.914 --> 00:15:50.279
It's taken years...

00:15:50.349 --> 00:15:53.284
for Seven to become
an individual.

00:15:53.352 --> 00:15:57.118
You're asking me to change
your son in one week?

00:15:57.189 --> 00:15:59.453
I'm sure you'll think
of something.

00:15:59.525 --> 00:16:00.423
What if she doesn't?

00:16:01.427 --> 00:16:04.954
Then it's single-cellular city
for you, my boy.

00:16:08.067 --> 00:16:09.762
I'm getting off this ship.

00:16:14.807 --> 00:16:18.072
Janeway to Security.

00:16:18.143 --> 00:16:19.906
What you no longer have, Q,

00:16:20.045 --> 00:16:23.242
is unlimited control
of space, matter and time,

00:16:23.315 --> 00:16:26.250
which means I give
the orders around here.

00:16:26.318 --> 00:16:27.979
Do I make myself clear?

00:16:29.688 --> 00:16:30.882
Your quarters.

00:16:41.333 --> 00:16:43.130
The petri dish was less cramped.

00:16:43.202 --> 00:16:44.794
Get some sleep...
you're going to need it.

00:16:44.870 --> 00:16:45.928
What for?

00:16:46.038 --> 00:16:47.335
I'm preparing a curriculum

00:16:47.406 --> 00:16:49.306
for you to follow
while you're here.

00:16:49.375 --> 00:16:53.471
You're going to learn respect
and responsibility.

00:16:53.545 --> 00:16:56.343
Don't tell me you're actually
going through with Q's plan.

00:16:56.415 --> 00:16:58.315
I may not approve
of his methods,

00:16:58.384 --> 00:17:01.615
but, for once, his heart
seems to be in the right place.

00:17:03.522 --> 00:17:05.820
I think his desire
to help you is genuine.

00:17:05.891 --> 00:17:09.987
He abandoned me on an antiquated
flying machine run by primates.

00:17:10.062 --> 00:17:13.463
We primates are your only hope.

00:17:17.002 --> 00:17:19.903
Seven days?

00:17:20.005 --> 00:17:21.302
How hard could it be?

00:17:27.012 --> 00:17:28.809
Seven of Nine will be
instructing you

00:17:28.881 --> 00:17:29.905
in spatial causality.

00:17:30.015 --> 00:17:31.505
You will learn how your actions

00:17:31.583 --> 00:17:33.278
can have widespread
repercussions.

00:17:33.352 --> 00:17:34.284
I read the padd.

00:17:34.353 --> 00:17:35.581
You're going to tell me

00:17:35.654 --> 00:17:39.090
how I can't create anomaly A
without causing phenomenon B,

00:17:39.158 --> 00:17:42.025
which, in turn, affects
civilization C, right?

00:17:45.697 --> 00:17:47.824
I'm... Icheb.

00:17:47.900 --> 00:17:48.832
Oh, I know who you are.

00:17:48.901 --> 00:17:50.493
You're the drone
with the Kirk fixation.

00:17:50.569 --> 00:17:53.060
You would be wise to follow
Icheb's example.

00:17:53.138 --> 00:17:54.127
By applying himself,

00:17:54.206 --> 00:17:56.333
he's become
a valued member of this crew.

00:17:56.408 --> 00:17:58.535
Can I see you naked again?

00:18:07.653 --> 00:18:11.111
Computer, run
Diplomacy Scenario 12-Alpha.

00:18:12.357 --> 00:18:14.257
The planetoid is
in Nausicaan space.

00:18:14.326 --> 00:18:15.418
It belongs to us now.

00:18:15.494 --> 00:18:16.586
After you.

00:18:16.662 --> 00:18:19.256
Come anywhere near it,
and we'll attack you.

00:18:19.331 --> 00:18:20.764
You can't intimidate us.

00:18:20.833 --> 00:18:23.734
We've as much right to mine
that dilithium as you do!

00:18:23.802 --> 00:18:26.771
What are you doing here,
Starfleet?

00:18:26.839 --> 00:18:29.501
Computer, freeze program.

00:18:29.575 --> 00:18:32.442
I assume you're familiar
with these species.

00:18:32.511 --> 00:18:35.344
Nausicaan,
Bolian, Cardassian, Romulan,

00:18:35.414 --> 00:18:37.348
Ferengi, and Bajoran.

00:18:37.416 --> 00:18:39.782
They're fighting over the
mining rights to a planetoid.

00:18:39.852 --> 00:18:41.717
Your job is
to settle the dispute.

00:18:41.787 --> 00:18:45.052
These aliens mean nothing to me.

00:18:45.124 --> 00:18:46.921
What do I care
if they can't get along?

00:18:47.025 --> 00:18:49.391
One of your
responsibilities as a Q

00:18:49.461 --> 00:18:52.521
is to maintain order
in the universe, right?

00:18:52.598 --> 00:18:53.895
So I've been told.

00:18:53.966 --> 00:18:58.130
Well, if you can't help these
races come to an agreement,

00:18:58.203 --> 00:18:59.227
there might be a war.

00:18:59.304 --> 00:19:01.636
The Alpha Quadrant
would be thrown into chaos.

00:19:02.841 --> 00:19:04.365
Why don't we try

00:19:04.443 --> 00:19:06.411
running the first scenario
together?

00:19:07.446 --> 00:19:10.040
I don't need your help.

00:19:10.115 --> 00:19:11.582
I can do this myself.

00:19:13.652 --> 00:19:15.381
If you want to try...

00:19:15.454 --> 00:19:16.580
be my guest.

00:19:16.655 --> 00:19:19.920
I'll be back in 30 minutes
to check on your progress.

00:19:20.993 --> 00:19:23.257
And... remember...

00:19:23.328 --> 00:19:25.626
Security is right outside.

00:19:29.668 --> 00:19:32.398
Computer, resume program.

00:19:32.471 --> 00:19:35.668
The planetoid
is in Nausicaan space.

00:19:35.741 --> 00:19:37.106
It belongs to us now.

00:19:37.176 --> 00:19:38.438
You can't intimidate us.

00:19:38.510 --> 00:19:41.536
We have as much right to mine
that dilithium as you do.

00:19:44.316 --> 00:19:46.375
Aren't you supposed
to be supervising

00:19:46.451 --> 00:19:47.577
our young guest?

00:19:47.653 --> 00:19:49.814
He says he doesn't
need supervision.

00:19:49.888 --> 00:19:51.253
And you accepted that?

00:19:51.323 --> 00:19:52.449
Of course not.

00:19:52.524 --> 00:19:54.583
I'm just giving him
the chance to fail.

00:19:54.660 --> 00:19:56.594
Then he'll have to ask
for some help.

00:19:56.662 --> 00:19:58.391
Sounds like a good strategy.

00:19:58.463 --> 00:20:00.397
Let me know how it goes.

00:20:05.270 --> 00:20:07.204
Settling the planetoid
predicament

00:20:07.272 --> 00:20:08.569
didn't take very long,

00:20:08.640 --> 00:20:11.939
so I used the rest of the time
to convince the Cardassian

00:20:12.010 --> 00:20:14.444
to apologize for the occupation
of Bajor.

00:20:14.513 --> 00:20:16.777
How's that for order
in the universe?

00:20:18.183 --> 00:20:19.480
Welcome.

00:20:19.551 --> 00:20:21.883
It's so nice to see you
this evening.

00:20:21.954 --> 00:20:23.148
I hope you're hungry.

00:20:23.222 --> 00:20:24.154
Step right up.

00:20:24.223 --> 00:20:26.054
There's plenty for everyone.

00:20:26.124 --> 00:20:27.489
Enjoy!

00:20:27.559 --> 00:20:28.651
Do you ever stop?

00:20:28.727 --> 00:20:31.787
Oh, I'm sorry.

00:20:31.863 --> 00:20:33.057
I forgot.

00:20:33.131 --> 00:20:35.565
My talking annoys you.

00:20:35.634 --> 00:20:37.261
Too bad you can't just...

00:20:38.503 --> 00:20:40.733
...shut me up again, huh?

00:20:40.806 --> 00:20:44.298
Crewman Biddle, where have
you been hiding yourself?

00:20:44.376 --> 00:20:45.809
I haven't seen you in days!

00:20:45.877 --> 00:20:46.969
If it isn't drone boy.

00:20:47.112 --> 00:20:48.477
You come to put me to sleep

00:20:48.547 --> 00:20:50.640
with another one
of your presentations?

00:20:50.716 --> 00:20:53.549
Actually, I was wondering
if you'd like to participate

00:20:53.619 --> 00:20:55.280
in some
recreational activities.

00:20:55.354 --> 00:20:56.616
I don't have the time.

00:20:56.688 --> 00:20:59.782
Aunt Kathy's forcing me
to write an historical essay

00:20:59.858 --> 00:21:00.984
on the Q Continuum.

00:21:01.059 --> 00:21:03.857
That's a challenging subject.

00:21:03.929 --> 00:21:06.056
I've never written
an essay before.

00:21:06.131 --> 00:21:07.826
I don't know where to start.

00:21:07.899 --> 00:21:10.561
The origin of the Q seems
like the most logical place,

00:21:10.636 --> 00:21:13.605
followed by an analysis of their
interaction with humanity.

00:21:13.672 --> 00:21:15.230
You could conclude
with a description

00:21:15.307 --> 00:21:16.934
of the events
that led you to Voyager.

00:21:17.075 --> 00:21:19.942
Would you mind writing
some of this down for me?

00:21:20.045 --> 00:21:21.376
I'll get a padd.

00:21:25.384 --> 00:21:28.945
Insightful, informative.

00:21:29.087 --> 00:21:30.384
I'm impressed.

00:21:30.455 --> 00:21:32.355
Too bad you didn't write it.

00:21:32.424 --> 00:21:33.914
What do you mean?

00:21:33.992 --> 00:21:37.723
I'd recognize Icheb's
style anywhere.

00:21:37.796 --> 00:21:42.256
He gave me a few notes
on my first draft, that's all.

00:21:42.334 --> 00:21:44.359
I negotiated a peace treaty

00:21:44.436 --> 00:21:48.338
between six belligerent species
in just 13 minutes.

00:21:48.407 --> 00:21:50.534
When Commander Chakotay
left the room,

00:21:50.609 --> 00:21:52.975
you altered their
personality subroutines

00:21:53.078 --> 00:21:54.739
to make them more agreeable.

00:21:54.813 --> 00:21:57.338
We may be common bipeds,

00:21:57.416 --> 00:22:01.216
but we're not stupid.

00:22:01.286 --> 00:22:03.220
Your training is over.

00:22:03.288 --> 00:22:04.550
Go back to your room

00:22:04.623 --> 00:22:06.284
and wait for your father
to return.

00:22:06.358 --> 00:22:07.347
If you don't help me,

00:22:07.426 --> 00:22:09.587
the Continuum
will turn me into an amoeba.

00:22:09.661 --> 00:22:11.458
I wanted to help you,

00:22:11.530 --> 00:22:13.930
but instead of trying
to live up to your potential,

00:22:14.032 --> 00:22:15.590
you cheated.

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:18.864
Do you think it's easy
to live up to my potential?

00:22:18.937 --> 00:22:22.873
I was supposed to be the savior
of the Q Continuum.

00:22:22.941 --> 00:22:26.570
Tell me, how do you save a race
that's already omnipotent?

00:22:26.645 --> 00:22:30.103
Those were the Qs' expectations,
not mine.

00:22:30.182 --> 00:22:32.707
All I asked was
that you make a sincere effort,

00:22:32.784 --> 00:22:34.752
but you weren't even
willing to try.

00:22:34.820 --> 00:22:36.720
Please, Aunt Kathy...

00:22:37.789 --> 00:22:40.223
you're my only hope.

00:22:40.292 --> 00:22:42.624
Well, I'm glad
you finally realize that.

00:22:44.329 --> 00:22:46.263
Now, if your motives are
sincere,

00:22:46.331 --> 00:22:48.731
I'm willing to give you
another chance.

00:22:48.800 --> 00:22:50.392
But step out of line again,

00:22:50.469 --> 00:22:52.767
and I'm through with you,
understood?

00:22:52.838 --> 00:22:53.896
Understood.

00:22:53.972 --> 00:22:55.269
Dismissed!

00:23:09.187 --> 00:23:12.850
Captain's Log, Stardate 54704.5.

00:23:12.924 --> 00:23:15.518
It's been four days since
my ultimatum to the young Q,

00:23:15.594 --> 00:23:17.619
and he appears
to be making progress.

00:23:17.696 --> 00:23:19.891
His instructors inform me
that he's taking on

00:23:19.965 --> 00:23:21.626
his assignments
with new determination,

00:23:21.700 --> 00:23:23.065
and he's made a concerted effort

00:23:23.135 --> 00:23:25.467
to be more courteous
to the crew.

00:23:25.537 --> 00:23:26.834
It's hard to believe this is

00:23:26.905 --> 00:23:29.874
the same brazen young man
that came aboard a few days ago.

00:23:29.941 --> 00:23:30.930
Captain?

00:23:31.042 --> 00:23:32.805
This is for you.

00:23:33.945 --> 00:23:36.106
It's a new draft of my essay.

00:23:36.181 --> 00:23:37.773
I know you didn't ask for one,

00:23:37.849 --> 00:23:41.148
but I felt I owed it to you
for giving me a second chance.

00:23:41.219 --> 00:23:45.952
"I, Q: An Insider's View
of the Continuum."

00:23:46.091 --> 00:23:48.457
If the essay is half as clever
as the title,

00:23:48.527 --> 00:23:49.858
I'm sure I'll enjoy it.

00:23:51.263 --> 00:23:55.825
Lieutenant Paris has offered
to give me a piloting lesson.

00:23:55.901 --> 00:23:56.868
I thought you might like
to join us.

00:23:56.935 --> 00:23:59.733
Oh, thanks, but I have
to help Crewman Chell

00:23:59.805 --> 00:24:01.705
scrub the plasma conduits.

00:24:01.773 --> 00:24:04.207
I think you've earned a break.

00:24:04.276 --> 00:24:06.540
This is the only time off
I'm giving you.

00:24:06.611 --> 00:24:08.545
I suggest
you take advantage of it.

00:24:08.613 --> 00:24:10.342
Yes, ma'am.

00:24:12.417 --> 00:24:13.543
Piloting lesson, huh?

00:24:13.618 --> 00:24:14.607
Where are we going?

00:24:21.126 --> 00:24:22.923
Steady...

00:24:23.028 --> 00:24:25.155
Ease up a little
on the thrusters.

00:24:27.399 --> 00:24:29.492
In case you forgot,
I'm mortal now.

00:24:29.568 --> 00:24:33.129
I'd appreciate it if you didn't
fly us into a rock.

00:24:33.205 --> 00:24:36.436
Maybe Q could take over
for a little while.

00:24:36.508 --> 00:24:37.770
What do you say?

00:24:37.843 --> 00:24:39.367
You want a turn at the wheel?

00:24:39.444 --> 00:24:42.208
Ordinarily, a Q
wouldn't demean himself

00:24:42.280 --> 00:24:44.544
by operating
primitive machinery,

00:24:44.616 --> 00:24:47.517
but these aren't
ordinary circumstances.

00:24:55.060 --> 00:24:56.721
Uh, did I do something wrong?

00:24:56.795 --> 00:24:59.423
Just a little ion imbalance
in the impulse drive.

00:24:59.498 --> 00:25:00.897
Nothing to worry about.

00:25:00.966 --> 00:25:02.831
Well, it's very distracting.

00:25:02.901 --> 00:25:04.334
Can't you fix it?

00:25:04.402 --> 00:25:06.734
Well, I could, but we'd have
to go back to Voyager

00:25:06.805 --> 00:25:07.737
and run diagnostics.

00:25:07.806 --> 00:25:09.740
If you two don't mind
cutting your lesson

00:25:09.841 --> 00:25:11.502
a little short.

00:25:13.311 --> 00:25:14.471
That won't be necessary.

00:25:14.546 --> 00:25:16.173
In fact,
I barely hear it anymore.

00:25:16.248 --> 00:25:17.180
Do you hear it?

00:25:17.249 --> 00:25:18.614
Hear what?

00:25:24.789 --> 00:25:26.086
Going up?

00:25:26.157 --> 00:25:27.146
I'll catch the next one.

00:25:27.225 --> 00:25:29.216
Hmm.

00:25:37.969 --> 00:25:40.164
Oh, you can't get away
from me that easily.

00:25:40.238 --> 00:25:41.364
It's only been five days.

00:25:41.439 --> 00:25:42.667
Why are you back?

00:25:42.741 --> 00:25:45.301
Oh, I thought I'd just pop in
and check on Junior.

00:25:45.377 --> 00:25:47.845
I'm not an entirely uninvolved
father, you know.

00:25:47.913 --> 00:25:49.881
Well, he got off
to a pretty shaky start,

00:25:49.948 --> 00:25:51.882
but he's made some progress
since then.

00:25:51.950 --> 00:25:53.247
Really!

00:25:53.318 --> 00:25:55.218
He's been working
extremely hard.

00:25:55.287 --> 00:25:56.879
We're talking about the same Q?

00:25:56.955 --> 00:25:58.217
If you don't believe me,

00:25:58.290 --> 00:26:00.315
maybe you should
see for yourself.

00:26:01.960 --> 00:26:05.396
The Continuum has been perceived
in a variety of ways...

00:26:05.463 --> 00:26:06.725
a dreary desert road,

00:26:06.798 --> 00:26:08.493
a blood-soaked battleground...

00:26:08.567 --> 00:26:10.626
but with the help
of Voyager's crew,

00:26:10.702 --> 00:26:13.569
I've begun to perceive it
in another context... a home.

00:26:13.638 --> 00:26:14.900
I look forward to the day

00:26:15.006 --> 00:26:17.099
when I return there
and make that perception

00:26:17.175 --> 00:26:19.837
a reality.

00:26:22.447 --> 00:26:23.914
Well?

00:26:23.982 --> 00:26:25.279
Huh?

00:26:25.350 --> 00:26:26.783
What did you think?

00:26:26.851 --> 00:26:28.512
Oh, it's very nice.

00:26:28.587 --> 00:26:29.451
Nice?

00:26:29.521 --> 00:26:30.613
Yes, I especially liked

00:26:30.689 --> 00:26:32.122
the part about the Continuum.

00:26:32.190 --> 00:26:35.921
The entire essay
was about the Continuum.

00:26:36.027 --> 00:26:39.019
Yes, and it's very nice.

00:26:39.097 --> 00:26:41.361
I'm late for my
temporal mechanics lesson.

00:26:41.433 --> 00:26:43.765
Q...

00:26:43.835 --> 00:26:46.497
Well, if there's nothing else,
I'll be on my way.

00:26:46.571 --> 00:26:47.902
He worked so hard
on that paper.

00:26:47.973 --> 00:26:49.235
The least you could have done

00:26:49.307 --> 00:26:50.797
was tell him
you were proud of him.

00:26:50.875 --> 00:26:52.103
But I'm not.

00:26:53.545 --> 00:26:55.069
And frankly, it's a little hard

00:26:55.146 --> 00:26:57.876
to be impressed with any
of the boy's accomplishments.

00:26:57.949 --> 00:27:00.884
He's been here for five days,
and what have you taught him?

00:27:00.952 --> 00:27:03.443
How to scribble essays
and play with holograms.

00:27:03.521 --> 00:27:05.011
What's next, basket weaving?

00:27:05.090 --> 00:27:06.785
Whether you're willing
to admit it or not,

00:27:06.858 --> 00:27:08.189
your son has made progress here.

00:27:08.259 --> 00:27:09.487
He has the potential

00:27:09.561 --> 00:27:11.119
to be a better Q
than you will ever be.

00:27:11.196 --> 00:27:14.029
Potential isn't going to be
enough for the Continuum.

00:27:14.099 --> 00:27:15.623
Then what will be enough?

00:27:15.700 --> 00:27:18.362
The boy needs to demonstrate
nothing less than...

00:27:18.436 --> 00:27:19.835
exemplary Q-ness.

00:27:19.904 --> 00:27:22.168
And what exactly is Q-ness?

00:27:22.240 --> 00:27:24.333
Oh, it's impossible
for your minuscule mind

00:27:24.409 --> 00:27:27.674
to comprehend,
but I know Q-ness when I see it,

00:27:27.746 --> 00:27:29.646
and this...

00:27:29.714 --> 00:27:31.511
is not it.

00:27:47.465 --> 00:27:48.727
Come in.

00:27:50.869 --> 00:27:53.429
I wanted to see how you were.

00:27:55.106 --> 00:27:57.097
I'm perfectly fine.

00:27:57.175 --> 00:27:59.075
Why wouldn't I be?

00:27:59.144 --> 00:28:03.046
I thought you might be upset
by Q's reaction to your essay.

00:28:05.316 --> 00:28:07.307
He's impossible to please.

00:28:07.385 --> 00:28:09.546
I don't care what he thinks.

00:28:14.726 --> 00:28:16.250
We have two days left.

00:28:16.327 --> 00:28:18.295
Let's make the most of them.

00:28:22.167 --> 00:28:23.634
Aunt Kathy...

00:28:23.702 --> 00:28:25.294
do you think the Continuum

00:28:25.370 --> 00:28:28.237
will be any more impressed
with me than Q was?

00:28:30.475 --> 00:28:33.035
That's what I thought.

00:28:35.714 --> 00:28:39.673
If the Continuum decides
they won't take you back,

00:28:39.751 --> 00:28:42.549
I'll ask them
to let you stay here.

00:28:42.620 --> 00:28:46.386
I don't think they care
where an amoeba spends eternity.

00:28:46.458 --> 00:28:49.291
That's not what I meant.

00:28:49.360 --> 00:28:52.989
I'll ask them to let
you remain human.

00:28:55.500 --> 00:28:58.298
I appreciate that...

00:28:58.369 --> 00:29:01.634
but I don't want to be human.

00:29:01.706 --> 00:29:05.574
I want to be a Q...

00:29:05.643 --> 00:29:08.635
like my father.

00:29:17.055 --> 00:29:21.321
Itchy! Are you in here? Ltchy?

00:29:21.392 --> 00:29:24.327
What can I do for you, Q-Ball?

00:29:24.395 --> 00:29:26.022
I need your help.

00:29:30.401 --> 00:29:33.029
Remember that ion imbalance
Lieutenant Paris mentioned

00:29:33.104 --> 00:29:34.696
during our lesson?

00:29:34.773 --> 00:29:36.741
We're going
to repair it for him.

00:29:36.808 --> 00:29:38.298
Did you get permission?

00:29:38.376 --> 00:29:39.741
Well, that would ruin
the surprise.

00:29:39.811 --> 00:29:41.039
The surprise?!

00:29:41.112 --> 00:29:42.579
The Captain's
been encouraging me

00:29:42.647 --> 00:29:43.909
to take more initiative.

00:29:43.982 --> 00:29:46.177
I want to show her
I can do things for others

00:29:46.251 --> 00:29:48.242
without being asked.

00:29:48.319 --> 00:29:50.810
I'll help you, on one condition.

00:29:50.889 --> 00:29:51.878
Name it.

00:29:51.956 --> 00:29:53.617
You won't refer to me as "ltchy"

00:29:53.691 --> 00:29:55.420
in front of the senior officers.

00:29:59.230 --> 00:30:02.666
I've realigned the last pair
of power couplings.

00:30:02.734 --> 00:30:05.430
You can start
the preignition sequence.

00:30:05.503 --> 00:30:06.970
Understood.

00:30:09.607 --> 00:30:14.442
I'm not detecting
any ion fluctuations.

00:30:14.512 --> 00:30:15.945
We did it.

00:30:16.080 --> 00:30:18.378
You can power down
the engine now.

00:30:21.352 --> 00:30:22.842
Q?

00:30:24.289 --> 00:30:25.847
What are you doing?

00:30:25.924 --> 00:30:28.290
You're gonna love this.

00:30:28.359 --> 00:30:30.520
I once learned how
to open a spatial flexure,

00:30:30.595 --> 00:30:32.688
using nothing more
than a deflector array.

00:30:32.764 --> 00:30:34.755
"Flexure"?

00:30:34.833 --> 00:30:36.892
It's like a tunnel
through space.

00:30:36.968 --> 00:30:39.766
I'm going to open one
to the Clevari system.

00:30:39.838 --> 00:30:41.100
Just wait
till you see the females.

00:30:41.172 --> 00:30:42.298
They're spectacular.

00:30:42.373 --> 00:30:45.206
We need the Captain's permission
to leave Voyager.

00:30:45.276 --> 00:30:47.073
Do you think
she'd give it to us?

00:30:47.145 --> 00:30:48.635
No.

00:30:48.713 --> 00:30:50.738
Then there's no point in asking.

00:30:50.815 --> 00:30:52.749
You've been doing so well.

00:30:52.817 --> 00:30:54.614
Why break the rules now?

00:30:54.686 --> 00:30:57.246
I'm bored.

00:30:57.322 --> 00:30:59.119
Icheb to Security.

00:30:59.190 --> 00:31:00.452
They can't hear you.

00:31:00.525 --> 00:31:02.550
I've dampened
all outgoing communications.

00:31:06.164 --> 00:31:08.223
Just sit back, ltchy.

00:31:08.299 --> 00:31:10.733
Enjoy the ride.

00:31:19.544 --> 00:31:22.069
What's the real reason
you're doing this?

00:31:22.146 --> 00:31:23.408
I'm getting out of here

00:31:23.481 --> 00:31:25.676
before my father can put me
back in that petri dish.

00:31:25.750 --> 00:31:27.115
The Q are omnipotent.

00:31:27.185 --> 00:31:28.447
They'll find you.

00:31:28.519 --> 00:31:32.148
I may not have my powers
anymore, but I know plenty

00:31:32.223 --> 00:31:35.420
of cosmic nooks and crannies
we can hide in.

00:31:35.493 --> 00:31:38.519
Voyager has locked onto us
with a tractor beam.

00:31:38.596 --> 00:31:40.496
They're so predictable.

00:31:42.200 --> 00:31:45.431
They're opening some sort of
spatial rift off their port bow.

00:31:45.503 --> 00:31:47.528
It's disrupting
the tractor beam.

00:31:47.605 --> 00:31:49.436
Compensate.

00:31:56.781 --> 00:31:58.612
They're gone.

00:32:11.996 --> 00:32:15.659
Welcome to the Clevari system.

00:32:15.733 --> 00:32:18.531
What would you like to do first?

00:32:18.603 --> 00:32:20.935
Take a dip with
the mermaids of Golos Prime?

00:32:21.005 --> 00:32:23.166
Challenge the warrior goddess
of Fekdar

00:32:23.241 --> 00:32:24.503
to a grappling contest?

00:32:24.575 --> 00:32:26.634
What I want is
to return to Voyager.

00:32:26.711 --> 00:32:30.272
Forget that dreary ship,
with its rules and regulations.

00:32:30.348 --> 00:32:32.407
We can do anything we want here.

00:32:32.483 --> 00:32:33.472
Go back to Voyager.

00:32:33.551 --> 00:32:34.950
Apologize to the Captain.

00:32:35.019 --> 00:32:35.951
She'll help you.

00:32:36.020 --> 00:32:36.952
It's too late.

00:32:37.021 --> 00:32:38.682
She said one more violation,

00:32:38.756 --> 00:32:40.451
I'll be thrown off her ship.

00:32:40.525 --> 00:32:42.425
I'm pretty sure this qualifies.

00:32:45.530 --> 00:32:46.963
What's wrong?

00:32:47.031 --> 00:32:48.828
There's a vessel approaching.

00:32:52.937 --> 00:32:55.531
You're trespassing
in Chokuzan space.

00:32:55.606 --> 00:32:56.868
We were just leaving.

00:32:56.941 --> 00:32:59.273
Our laws require
that you be incarcerated,

00:32:59.344 --> 00:33:00.777
pending an investigation.

00:33:00.845 --> 00:33:02.642
How long will that take?

00:33:02.714 --> 00:33:07.276
Disengage your engines
and prepare to be boarded.

00:33:07.352 --> 00:33:09.377
We should do as he says.

00:33:09.454 --> 00:33:12.617
Why, just because
he has a bigger ship?

00:33:12.690 --> 00:33:15.215
Because Captain Janeway has
taught us to respect the laws

00:33:15.293 --> 00:33:16.920
of other cultures.

00:33:16.995 --> 00:33:19.759
I should have known better
than to bring you along.

00:33:26.170 --> 00:33:27.865
You're going to get us killed!

00:33:27.939 --> 00:33:29.429
Did you expect me to surrender?

00:33:29.507 --> 00:33:31.270
He might have
locked us up for years.

00:33:31.342 --> 00:33:33.207
You don't know that.

00:33:33.277 --> 00:33:34.744
There's no time for a debate.

00:33:34.812 --> 00:33:36.279
I need you at Tactical.

00:33:41.152 --> 00:33:43.916
Shields are down to 30 percent.

00:33:43.988 --> 00:33:46.252
Sixteen percent.

00:33:46.324 --> 00:33:47.586
I'm opening another flexure!

00:33:47.658 --> 00:33:48.955
We'll go to the Zozek system.

00:33:49.093 --> 00:33:50.526
The girls aren't as attractive,

00:33:50.595 --> 00:33:52.460
but we have to make
some compromises.

00:33:59.871 --> 00:34:03.102
Icheb!

00:34:03.174 --> 00:34:05.665
I'm detecting
another rift forming...

00:34:05.743 --> 00:34:09.235
approximately 5,000 kilometers
directly ahead.

00:34:09.313 --> 00:34:10.803
A vessel is emerging.

00:34:10.882 --> 00:34:12.315
It's the Flyer.

00:34:12.383 --> 00:34:13.509
They're hailing.

00:34:13.584 --> 00:34:15.484
- On screen.
- Aunt Kathy...

00:34:15.553 --> 00:34:17.111
Don't you "Aunt Kathy" me.

00:34:17.188 --> 00:34:18.155
Yell at me later.

00:34:18.222 --> 00:34:19.621
We need to get Icheb
to Sick Bay.

00:34:23.494 --> 00:34:25.359
His cells are being necrotized

00:34:25.430 --> 00:34:27.625
by some form
of omicron radiation,

00:34:27.698 --> 00:34:30.929
but I can't treat his injuries
without knowing more

00:34:31.002 --> 00:34:33.835
about the weapon
that caused them.

00:34:33.905 --> 00:34:35.497
Is this a bad time?

00:34:35.573 --> 00:34:37.473
Tell him.

00:34:39.010 --> 00:34:41.843
Icheb stole a shuttle
from Voyager.

00:34:41.913 --> 00:34:44.473
I tried to stop him,
but he kidnapped me,

00:34:44.549 --> 00:34:45.948
and he started a fight
with another ship.

00:34:46.017 --> 00:34:47.279
He stole the shuttle,

00:34:47.351 --> 00:34:49.046
and he attacked
the other vessel.

00:34:49.120 --> 00:34:50.382
Is that true, son?

00:34:52.457 --> 00:34:54.687
Please, Q, just save him.

00:34:54.759 --> 00:34:55.817
Don't be absurd.

00:34:55.893 --> 00:34:57.656
You're not going to help him?

00:34:57.728 --> 00:34:58.854
Like Aunt Kathy said,

00:34:58.930 --> 00:35:00.397
you're never going
to learn anything

00:35:00.465 --> 00:35:03.491
if you don't face the
consequences of your actions.

00:35:03.568 --> 00:35:07.060
If your little playmate has
to die to teach you a lesson,

00:35:07.138 --> 00:35:09.299
so be it.

00:35:14.912 --> 00:35:16.209
I know you can hear me, Q.

00:35:16.280 --> 00:35:19.010
Come back! Q!

00:35:19.083 --> 00:35:20.641
You're wasting your time.

00:35:20.718 --> 00:35:23.278
He's the only one
who can save Icheb.

00:35:23.354 --> 00:35:24.844
No, he isn't.

00:35:26.557 --> 00:35:28.787
You're going back
to that ship you attacked.

00:35:28.860 --> 00:35:31.021
You're going to apologize
for what you did,

00:35:31.095 --> 00:35:32.892
and you're going
to plead with them

00:35:32.964 --> 00:35:35.694
for the information we need
to save Icheb.

00:35:35.766 --> 00:35:37.131
Look at what they did to him.

00:35:37.201 --> 00:35:39.135
If I go back,
they'll do the same to me.

00:35:39.203 --> 00:35:40.363
What do you care?

00:35:40.438 --> 00:35:42.463
By this time tomorrow,
you'll be an amoeba.

00:35:42.540 --> 00:35:44.303
Well, I'd rather be an amoeba
than a corpse!

00:35:44.375 --> 00:35:45.637
That would be easier,

00:35:45.710 --> 00:35:46.938
wouldn't it?

00:35:47.044 --> 00:35:48.636
No expectations to live up to.

00:35:48.713 --> 00:35:50.203
No one to disappoint.

00:35:52.517 --> 00:35:55.111
I'm a failure as a Q
and a human.

00:35:55.186 --> 00:35:58.883
If I'm a single-celled organism,
at least I can't hurt anybody.

00:35:58.956 --> 00:36:01.356
Why did you come back here?

00:36:01.425 --> 00:36:04.028
To escape the Chokuzan.

00:36:04.095 --> 00:36:05.790
You could've
used your technology

00:36:05.863 --> 00:36:10.300
to take you anywhere,
but you came back here to us.

00:36:10.368 --> 00:36:11.630
Why?

00:36:11.702 --> 00:36:14.762
I probably hit
the wrong control.

00:36:17.975 --> 00:36:20.466
Icheb is the only friend
I've ever had.

00:36:20.545 --> 00:36:21.910
I brought him back here,

00:36:22.046 --> 00:36:24.139
because I thought
you could save him.

00:36:24.215 --> 00:36:25.705
Obviously, I was mistaken.

00:36:25.783 --> 00:36:28.547
The only mistake you made
was running away.

00:36:28.619 --> 00:36:31.486
You have a chance
to do the right thing now.

00:36:31.556 --> 00:36:33.023
Don't waste it.

00:36:41.132 --> 00:36:44.226
The attack on your vessel
was entirely my fault.

00:36:44.302 --> 00:36:48.363
Icheb had nothing to do with it,
but he's the one who's dying.

00:36:48.439 --> 00:36:51.374
I-I take full responsibility
for what happened.

00:36:51.442 --> 00:36:53.637
I'll do anything you ask.

00:36:53.711 --> 00:36:55.440
Just help my friend.

00:36:55.513 --> 00:36:58.414
My crew and I will repair
any damage he did

00:36:58.482 --> 00:36:59.779
to your ship.

00:36:59.850 --> 00:37:01.977
Are you the adult
responsible for this child?

00:37:05.356 --> 00:37:07.517
I suppose I am.

00:37:08.826 --> 00:37:10.453
We'll accept his apology

00:37:10.528 --> 00:37:15.465
and give you the information
you need to save his accomplice,

00:37:15.533 --> 00:37:20.903
but you will be punished
for their crime.

00:37:21.038 --> 00:37:23.404
She didn't have anything
to do with it.

00:37:23.474 --> 00:37:25.442
In our culture,
adults are accountable

00:37:25.509 --> 00:37:27.272
for the actions
of their children.

00:37:27.345 --> 00:37:29.074
I attacked your ship.

00:37:29.146 --> 00:37:32.206
I should be punished for it,
not her.

00:37:32.283 --> 00:37:34.808
You don't even know
what the punishment is.

00:37:34.885 --> 00:37:37.820
It might be torture,
or even execution.

00:37:37.888 --> 00:37:39.321
I don't care,

00:37:39.390 --> 00:37:41.790
if it means saving my friend.

00:37:47.565 --> 00:37:49.760
Well done, Junior.

00:37:51.369 --> 00:37:53.428
I'm proud of you.

00:37:53.504 --> 00:37:56.302
Surprise!

00:37:57.808 --> 00:37:59.833
I wish you could see the look
on your faces.

00:37:59.910 --> 00:38:02.208
Oh, wait. You can.

00:38:03.914 --> 00:38:05.643
We don't have time
for your games.

00:38:05.716 --> 00:38:07.980
We need to find
the real people I attacked.

00:38:08.052 --> 00:38:09.451
You just did.

00:38:09.520 --> 00:38:11.852
I was the Chokuzan you fired on.

00:38:11.922 --> 00:38:14.516
What kind of horrible joke?

00:38:14.592 --> 00:38:16.617
Not a joke. A test.

00:38:16.694 --> 00:38:18.161
I knew the pathetic
little exercises

00:38:18.229 --> 00:38:21.096
you had him performing
would not impress the Continuum.

00:38:21.165 --> 00:38:26.296
So, when he escaped your
clutches, I devised a real test.

00:38:26.370 --> 00:38:28.861
It was touch and go there
for a moment,

00:38:28.939 --> 00:38:30.907
but you passed
with flying colors.

00:38:31.008 --> 00:38:33.033
What about Icheb?

00:38:33.110 --> 00:38:36.011
Your Doctor will discover
he's made a miraculous recovery.

00:38:36.080 --> 00:38:38.810
Now then,
if we're all finished here,

00:38:38.883 --> 00:38:41.147
it's Judgment Day for Junior.

00:38:49.160 --> 00:38:51.560
We're ready, Your Honor.

00:38:51.629 --> 00:38:55.497
In the case
of The Continuum vs. Q,

00:38:55.566 --> 00:38:57.363
we, the Continuum, have found

00:38:57.435 --> 00:38:59.767
that Q has not
made sufficient progress

00:38:59.837 --> 00:39:02.670
to warrant the reinstatement
of his powers.

00:39:02.740 --> 00:39:04.833
Objection.
What about my test?

00:39:04.909 --> 00:39:06.877
What about it?

00:39:06.944 --> 00:39:09.037
Q was willing to sacrifice
himself to save his friend.

00:39:09.113 --> 00:39:11.547
Surely that counts
for something.

00:39:11.615 --> 00:39:13.412
It was Q who endangered
the boy's life

00:39:13.484 --> 00:39:14.416
in the first place.

00:39:14.485 --> 00:39:17.477
However, in deference

00:39:17.555 --> 00:39:20.115
to the aforementioned
act of contrition,

00:39:20.191 --> 00:39:22.625
the defendant will not
be transformed

00:39:22.693 --> 00:39:24.354
into an Oprelian amoeba.

00:39:24.428 --> 00:39:25.656
Oh, good.

00:39:25.730 --> 00:39:27.561
Instead...

00:39:27.631 --> 00:39:30.464
he will suffer
the next worst fate...

00:39:30.534 --> 00:39:32.661
remaining human.

00:39:37.708 --> 00:39:40.142
Court is adjourned.

00:39:41.612 --> 00:39:43.910
This is an outrage!

00:39:44.014 --> 00:39:46.744
They can't do this to me!

00:40:01.599 --> 00:40:03.726
Come in.

00:40:03.801 --> 00:40:05.860
Do you have a moment?

00:40:08.706 --> 00:40:13.040
A few days ago, you offered
to let me remain on Voyager.

00:40:13.110 --> 00:40:15.237
I know I've made
a few mistakes since then,

00:40:15.312 --> 00:40:17.303
and you probably
don't want me around,

00:40:17.381 --> 00:40:19.281
but if it's all right

00:40:19.350 --> 00:40:23.218
with you... I'd like
to continue my training.

00:40:23.287 --> 00:40:26.222
But you have nothing left
to prove to the Continuum.

00:40:27.525 --> 00:40:29.550
But there's a lot
I still need to prove to you.

00:40:31.328 --> 00:40:32.886
What about your father?

00:40:35.800 --> 00:40:38.098
You don't honestly believe
we'll see him again, do you?

00:40:38.169 --> 00:40:39.966
He obviously doesn't
want me around.

00:40:40.070 --> 00:40:42.436
Why else would he have
left me here... twice?

00:40:44.141 --> 00:40:46.166
The question
you should be asking

00:40:46.243 --> 00:40:47.767
is why I keep coming back.

00:40:47.845 --> 00:40:50.575
Now, I'm sorry
I left so abruptly,

00:40:50.648 --> 00:40:53.515
but the Continuum's verdict
demanded an immediate appeal.

00:40:53.584 --> 00:40:55.848
I told them I refuse to belong

00:40:55.920 --> 00:41:00.289
to any Continuum that wouldn't
accept my son as a member.

00:41:00.357 --> 00:41:02.188
We're a package deal.

00:41:02.259 --> 00:41:04.420
You left the Continuum for me?

00:41:04.495 --> 00:41:05.427
Oh, don't be ridiculous.

00:41:05.496 --> 00:41:07.361
I'm the only one holding
that place together.

00:41:07.431 --> 00:41:09.831
And when they realized
they might lose me,

00:41:09.900 --> 00:41:12.528
they crumbled like a
Gelbian sand sculpture.

00:41:14.205 --> 00:41:15.866
They're going
to return my powers?

00:41:15.940 --> 00:41:17.237
They already have.

00:41:20.511 --> 00:41:25.505
For you, Captain,
for all your help.

00:41:25.583 --> 00:41:26.811
Thank you.

00:41:29.787 --> 00:41:31.687
Now that you're a Q again,

00:41:31.755 --> 00:41:34.121
I thought we might spend
some quality time together.

00:41:34.191 --> 00:41:38.093
I want to show you the cosmos
the way it was meant to be seen.

00:41:38.162 --> 00:41:39.390
We've tried that already.

00:41:39.463 --> 00:41:41.931
Things will be different
this time.

00:41:41.999 --> 00:41:43.193
I promise.

00:41:45.936 --> 00:41:47.301
Now run along.

00:41:47.371 --> 00:41:50.829
I'll meet you on Golos Prime.

00:41:50.908 --> 00:41:54.173
After I've had a few moments
alone with the Captain.

00:41:54.245 --> 00:41:55.803
I'll see you soon, Aunt Kathy.

00:41:55.880 --> 00:41:57.677
I certainly hope so.

00:42:00.451 --> 00:42:04.217
So, the Continuum "crumbled
like a Gelbian sand sculpture."

00:42:04.288 --> 00:42:06.313
Yes.

00:42:06.390 --> 00:42:07.857
Some of them even
got on their knees

00:42:07.925 --> 00:42:08.857
and begged me to stay.

00:42:08.926 --> 00:42:11.258
It was pathetic.

00:42:13.931 --> 00:42:15.262
If you must know,

00:42:15.332 --> 00:42:17.857
I had to agree
to a few minor conditions.

00:42:17.935 --> 00:42:19.698
Oh? Such as?

00:42:19.770 --> 00:42:21.738
Eternal custody of the boy.

00:42:23.440 --> 00:42:25.271
Wherever the little brat goes,
I go with him.

00:42:25.342 --> 00:42:28.140
I hope he won't spoil
too much of your fun.

00:42:29.747 --> 00:42:32.215
Oh, before I leave,

00:42:32.283 --> 00:42:35.081
I did a little homework for you.

00:42:35.152 --> 00:42:36.710
Consider it a thank you

00:42:36.787 --> 00:42:39.051
for everything you did
for Junior.

00:42:39.123 --> 00:42:41.216
Not that I don't appreciate it,

00:42:41.292 --> 00:42:44.261
but this will only take
a few years off our journey.

00:42:44.328 --> 00:42:47.229
Why not send us all the way?

00:42:48.832 --> 00:42:51.960
What sort of an example
would I be setting for my son

